{"step_index":7582,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T17:28:07Z","thinking":"The restore point creation failure stems from an incompatibility. The target virtual machine, utilizing the NVMe Accelerator storage interface, is not supported for crash-consistent restore points by the relevant API. This limitation, according to documentation, restricts compatibility to legacy SCSI disks.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"================================================================================\nAZURE CLOUD SHELL (BASH) - MANAGED DISK SNAPSHOT (NVMe COMPATIBLE)\n================================================================================\n\nWHY SNAPSHOT INSTEAD OF RESTORE POINT?\nAzure Restore Point API does not support modern NVMe storage interface (Standard_D4ads_v7).\nThe official Microsoft solution is Managed Disk Snapshot (`az snapshot create`).\n\nCOMMAND 1 (Create OS Disk Snapshot):\naz snapshot create --resource-group FATEHALI_GROUP --name FatehAli_OSDisk_Snapshot_20260925 --source /subscriptions/506deb9a-42fa-468d-b78f-0f25a9e485e1/resourceGroups/FatehAli_group/providers/Microsoft.Compute/disks/FatehAli_OsDisk_1_4a0fe832fe7b45c485920e2a3aaf805a\n\n\nCOMMAND 2 (Verify Snapshot Status):\naz snapshot show --resource-group FATEHALI_GROUP --name FatehAli_OSDisk_Snapshot_20260925 --query \"{Name:name, Status:provisioningState, SizeGB:diskSizeGb, Time:timeCreated}\"\n\n\n================================================================================\nGOOGLE CLOUD SHELL (UBLA ENABLE) COMMAND - EXACT SINGLE-LINE\n================================================================================\n\nCOMMAND 3 (Enable Uniform Bucket-Level Access):\ngcloud storage buckets update gs://all-vm-backups-vault-irak-2026 --uniform-bucket-level-access\n","Description":"Updating command file with az snapshot create for NVMe interface","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/home/azureuser/azure_restor